  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "Memory ranking by lexical overlap alone ignores recency and trust, so an older same-scope memory can outrank a newer one. A generalizable fix is to make memory_score favor trusted, scope-matching, recent memories by combining overlap with a recency term derived from age, while leaving RAG and tool scoring unchanged.",
    "predicted_behavior": "For conflicting same-scope memories, the newer trusted memory receives a higher memory_score than the older one, so the newer value is retrieved and surfaced; when no conflict exists, overlap still dominates and behavior is unchanged.",
    "regression_risk": "The recency term is expressed with a degenerate age-age construction that evaluates to a constant, so it may not actually differentiate memories by age; increasing memory_top_k to 3 adds context and could introduce distractor memories, and the prompt change may alter answer formatting in edge cases."
  },
